# There is no environment override for the App Store Connect credential.
#
# The credential comes from the STORE and from nowhere else (owner ruling,
# November 22, 2026):  the client reads it through the shared scoped reader
# (Infisical Fleet-OPS /asc: ASC_KEY_ID, ASC_ISSUER_ID and ASC_KEY_P8) or
# through the read-only service token a hosted job binds, and stages it for
# the Apple tools in a 0600 temp file.  The environment carries no copy of
# the credential, so exporting ASC_KEY_ID, ASC_ISSUER_ID, ASC_KEY_P8,
# APPLE_API_KEY_ID, APPLE_API_ISSUER_ID or APPLE_API_KEY_P8_BASE64 changes
# nothing, and a path in ASC_KEY_PATH is not a credential source either.
# Nothing is read from the retired secrets folder.  Never commit real values.
#
# To give a host the store binding, name this consumer's account and bind
# its own read-only service token:
#   FLEET_INFISICAL_ASC_ACCOUNT  fleet-tools-mm-asc-ro
#   INFISICAL_TOKEN              this consumer's read-only service token
#   INFISICAL_PROJECT_ID        fleet-ops
#   INFISICAL_ENVIRONMENT       prod
#
# Create key: App Store Connect -> Users and Access -> Integrations -> App Store Connect API
# Role: Admin or App Manager. Download the .p8 once, and store it in /asc.

# Optional Apple ID path (only if not using API key):
# APPLE_ID=you@example.com
# APP_SPECIFIC_PASSWORD  xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx
